{0} force FAIL by default to avoid IMPORTANT message below.
#1: Equipment Setup 1
a. Connect the 3v3 pull up and connect the GND to the Bus Priate cable.
b. Connect the XXX lead to + of channel 1 on the PSU.
c. Connect the XXXX lead to + of channel 2 on the PSU.
d. Connect the VPWR lead to + of channel 3 on the PSU.
e. Connect the GND's of channel 1, 2 & 3 together.
e. Set the TENMA Programmable PSU power switch to on.
//CLICK_OK:
CONNECT: TENMAPSU
IF_NOT:
GOTO: #1: 

#2: Equipment Setup 2 & Configure the PSU
a. Connect the fan and motor).
b. fit the PCB to the Test bed.
c. Enter the PCB serial number.
COMMAND:  TENMAPSU OUT0
COMMAND: TENMAPSU OCP1
COMMAND: TENMAPSU OCPSET1:1.000
COMMAND: TENMAPSU OCPSET2:0.000
COMMAND: TENMAPSU VSET1:12.00
COMMAND: TENMAPSU ISET1:1.000
COMMAND: TENMAPSU VSET2:0.00
COMMAND: TENMAPSU ISET2:0.000
//CLICK_OK:

#3: Connect and Configure the Bus Pirate
CONNECT: BUS_PIRATE
IF_NOT:
GOTO: #3:
COMMAND: BUS_PIRATE m4
COMMAND: BUS_PIRATE 3
COMMAND: BUS_PIRATE W // sets the power rail to on, and drives a voltage to pin 5 C_PWR_ON
COMMAND: BUS_PIRATE P

#4: Power supply enabled.
COMMAND: TENMAPSU OUTCH1:1
CLICK_OK:

#5: Driver config
COMMAND: BUS_PIRATE {0x48 0x0A 0x80} {0x48 0x00 0xA3} {0x48 0x10 0x00} {0x48 0x1A 0x06} // configure the GPIO with without Array
COMMAND: BUS_PIRATE {0x20 0x3F 0x34 0x00} // set the DAC to minimun
COMMAND: BUS_PIRATE {0x48 0x1A 0x04} //Enable Driver 1
CLICK_OK:

#6: Test Driver 1 and test current measurement IC
COMMAND: BUS_PIRATE { 0x82 0x05 0x02 0xF1 } //Driver1CurrentConfig
SUB: READ_SENSOR_CurrentDriver1
The returned current is = %RESULT% 
RANGE: %RESULT% 2 0 // set the range as per TS014_TEST_SEQUENCER_scripts.docx 
SUB: TestPassOrFailCL2
IF_NOT:
IMPORTANT: This PCB is not reading  any current draw
CLICK_OK:

#7: Test Driver 2 and test current measurement IC
COMMAND: BUS_PIRATE { 0x48 0x1A 0x06 }//Disable the drivers
COMMAND: BUS_PIRATE { 0x48 0x1A 0x02 } //Enable driver 2
COMMAND: BUS_PIRATE { 0x80 0x05 0x02 0xF1 } //Driver2CurrentConfig
SUB: READ_SENSOR_CurrentDriver2
The returned current is = %RESULT% 
RANGE: %RESULT% 2 0 // set the range as per TS014_TEST_SEQUENCER_scripts.docx 
SUB: TestPassOrFailCL2
IF_NOT:
IMPORTANT: This PCB is not reading  any current draw
CLICK_OK:
COMMAND: BUS_PIRATE { 0x48 0x1A 0x06 } //Disable the drivers
COMMAND: BUS_PIRATE m4
COMMAND: BUS_PIRATE 3
COMMAND: BUS_PIRATE W // sets the power rail to on, and drives a voltage to pin 5 C_PWR_ON
COMMAND: BUS_PIRATE P

#8: Arm Test White
// TP 32 and 23 must be pull to GND for the LED output to be enable.
COMMAND: BUS_PIRATE {0x44 0x00 0x11} //Configure the arm GPIOs 
//COMMAND: BUS_PIRATE {0x48 0x0A 0x80} {0x48 0x00 0xA3} {0x48 0x10 0x00} {0x48 0x1A 0x06} // configure the GPIO with without Array
//COMMAND: BUS_PIRATE {0x20 0x3F 0x34 0x00} // set the DAC to minimun
COMMAND: BUS_PIRATE {0x44 0x0A 0xDD} // set the white LED to On
COMMAND: BUS_PIRATE {0x48 0x1A 0x00} // enable the Drivers
SUB: READ_SENSOR_CurrentDriver1
The returned current is = %RESULT% 
RANGE: %RESULT% 2 0 // set the range as per TS014_TEST_SEQUENCER_scripts.docx 
SUB: TestPassOrFailCL2
IF_NOT:
IMPORTANT: This PCB is not reading  any current draw
DELAY: 3000
COMMAND: BUS_PIRATE {0x48 0x1A 0x06}
PASS_FAIL:


#9: Arm test IR
// TP 32 and 23 must be pull to GND for the LED output to be enable.
COMMAND: BUS_PIRATE {0x44 0x00 0x11} //Configure the arm GPIOs 
//COMMAND: BUS_PIRATE {0x48 0x0A 0x80} {0x48 0x00 0xA3} {0x48 0x10 0x00} {0x48 0x1A 0x06} // configure the GPIO with without Array
//COMMAND: BUS_PIRATE {0x20 0x3F 0x34 0x00} // set the DAC to minimun
COMMAND: BUS_PIRATE {0x44 0x0A 0xBB} // set the IR LED to On
COMMAND: BUS_PIRATE {0x48 0x1A 0x00} // enable the Drivers
SUB: READ_SENSOR_CurrentDriver1
The returned current is = %RESULT% 
RANGE: %RESULT% 2 0 // set the range as per TS014_TEST_SEQUENCER_scripts.docx 
SUB: TestPassOrFailCL2
IF_NOT:
IMPORTANT: This PCB is not reading  any current draw
DELAY: 3000
COMMAND: BUS_PIRATE {0x48 0x1A 0x06}
PASS_FAIL:



#10: Arm test UV
// TP 32 and 23 must be pull to GND for the LED output to be enable.
COMMAND: BUS_PIRATE {0x44 0x00 0x11} //Configure the arm GPIOs 
//COMMAND: BUS_PIRATE {0x48 0x0A 0x80} {0x48 0x00 0xA3} {0x48 0x10 0x00} {0x48 0x1A 0x06} // configure the GPIO with without Array
//COMMAND: BUS_PIRATE {0x20 0x3F 0x34 0x00} // set the DAC to minimun
COMMAND: BUS_PIRATE {0x44 0x0A 0x77} // set the UV LED to On
COMMAND: BUS_PIRATE {0x48 0x1A 0x00} // enable the Drivers
SUB: READ_SENSOR_CurrentDriver1
The returned current is = %RESULT% 
RANGE: %RESULT% 2 0 // set the range as per TS014_TEST_SEQUENCER_scripts.docx 
SUB: TestPassOrFailCL2
IF_NOT:
IMPORTANT: This PCB is not reading  any current draw
DELAY: 3000
COMMAND: BUS_PIRATE {0x48 0x1A 0x06}
PASS_FAIL:

#11: Motor test
Motor is moving?
COMMAND: BUS_PIRATE { 0x48 0x00 0x00 0xBF } //Configure the GPIO, Sets Port A (Motor) and GPB6 (Wake) to Output.
COMMAND: BUS_PIRATE { 0x48 0x12 0x01 0x40 } //set the states, GPA0-tp14-tp9 High (Enable), GPA1-tp15 Low (Dir), GPB6 High (Wake).
COMMAND: BUS_PIRATE { 0x48 0x12 0x03 }// set the direction, Sets GPA1 High (Reverse) while keeping GPA0 (Enable) High.
COMMAND: BUS_PIRATE g // using the BUS Aux pin to PWM the stepper driver
COMMAND: BUS_PIRATE 1
COMMAND: BUS_PIRATE 50
CLICK_OK:
Motor changed direction? 
COMMAND: BUS_PIRATE {0x48 0x12 0x01 }// set the direction
CLICK_OK:
COMMAND: BUS_PIRATE g
COMMAND: BUS_PIRATE { 0x48 0x12 0x00 } //Sets GPA0 Low (Disable Driver).

#12: Fan test
COMMAND: BUS_PIRATE { 0x48 0x00 0xBF } { 0x48 0x12 0x40 } //Configure the GPIO
Check fan is at full power
DELAY: 3000
PASS_FAIL:
COMMAND: BUS_PIRATE { 0x5E 0x30 0x80}
check fan speed decreases 
CLICK_OK:
SUB: READ_SENSOR_Tach
The returned current is = %RESULT% 
RANGE: %RESULT% 55 5 // set the range as per TS014_TEST_SEQUENCER_scripts.docx 
SUB: TestPassOrFailCL2
IF_NOT:
IMPORTANT: This PCB is not reading the data from the fan-Tach
CLICK_OK:
COMMAND: BUS_PIRATE { 0x48 0x12 0x00 } Sets GPA0 Low (Disable Driver).
Check fan is off.
PASS_FAIL:
 

#13: Cam PSU test
//TP34
COMMAND: BUS_PIRATE { 0x48 0x00 0xBF } //Configure the GPA4 to Output
COMMAND: BUS_PIRATE { 0x48 0x00 0xBF } //Set GPA4 to High
check the LED turned on
PASS_FAIL:


#11: IMU Sensor
COMMAND: BUS_PIRATE { 0xD6 0x10 0x60 }// wake up the imu 
//COMMAND: BUS_PIRATE { 0xD6 0x28 [ 0xD7 r:6 }// read the imu 
SUB: READ_SENSOR_IMU
The returned current is = %RESULT% 
RANGE: %RESULT% 60 5 // set the range as per TS014_TEST_SEQUENCER_scripts.docx 
SUB: TestPassOrFailCL2
IF_NOT:
IMPORTANT: This PCB is not reading the data from the IMU
CLICK_OK:
move the PCB
CLICK_OK:
SUB: READ_SENSOR_IMU
The returned current is = %RESULT% 
check the result changes
PASS_FAIL:


#12: Hall Sensor test
COMMAND: BUS_PIRATE D //Read the voltage on the hall Sensor
READLINE: BUS_PIRATE Voltage
Check the returned Voltage is 3.3V 
Returned = %Voltage% 
PASS_FAIL:

#13: Hall Sensor activation
Move the magnet arm over the hall Sensor.
CLICK_OK:
Check the Voltage is below 0.5V
READLINE: BUS_PIRATE Voltage
Returned = %Voltage% 
PASS_FAIL:


#14: Test complete
IF: %FAILED% > 0
GOTO: #Failed:
ELSE: #Passed:

#Failed: A test failed
a. This PCB has failed to pass all Tests
b. Check the Log file for more details on the failed test(s).
IMPORTANT: This PCB has failed to pass all Tests
//DISPLAY: test_failed.png
CLICK_OK:
GOTO: #QUIT:

#Passed: Test's Complete
a. All tests instructions have been completed and a log file created.
b. Click OK to finish and power OFF.
//DISPLAY: AllTestsPassed.png
CLICK_OK:

#QUIT:
COMMAND: TENMAPSU VSET1:0.00
COMMAND: TENMAPSU ISET1:0.00
COMMAND: TENMAPSU VSET2:0.00
COMMAND: TENMAPSU ISET2:0.00
COMMAND: TENMAPSU OUT0
COMMAND: BUS_PIRATE #
